### 0. Register a new user
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/register \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
  }'

### 1. Login with email & password
### Generates a fresh RSA keypair, saves public_key & 5-min expires_at to DB, and returns the private_key
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
  }'

### 2. Verify Validity
### Copy the "private_key" string from the login response and paste it into the "private_key" field below.
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/verify \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "private_key": "<PASTE_YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY_HERE>"
  }'

### 3. Refresh Key Expiration
### Verifies the key pair matches and extends expires_at by another 5 minutes from now.
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/refresh \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "private_key": "<PASTE_YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY_HERE>"
  }'

### 4. Logout
### Removes/nullifies the public_key and expires_at fields from the database, immediately revoking access.
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/logout \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "private_key": "<PASTE_YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY_HERE>"
  }'

### 5. Verify After Logout (Negative Test - Should return 401 Unauthorized)
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/verify \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "private_key": "<PASTE_YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY_HERE>"
  }'
